Milky[ Quartz] is the white,[ translucent] to opaque variety of[ Quartz]. Though very common in nature, it is not used as a gemstone.
Colorless[ Quartz] with golden yellow[ Rut]ile inclusions, as hairlike growths within the gemstone, are known as[ Rutilated Quartz]. See the[ Rutilated Quartz] gemstone page for more details.
